# infra-utm-anon-egress configuration
# Copy to lab.conf and adjust. lab.conf is gitignored.

# --- Identity ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Prefix for all VM names in UTM. Deliberately different from the redteam lab's
# prefix so the two fleets can never collide in the same UTM instance.
LAB_PREFIX="anon"

# User created inside every VM (cloud-init). Ansible connects as this user.
# Avoid a name that is already a system group in the guest: Debian and Kali
# ship legacy groups like operator (GID 37), staff, games and users. The
# cloud-init template handles the clash, but a free name keeps it simple.
LAB_USER="anon"

# Public SSH key injected into every VM. Generated automatically by
# scripts/preflight.sh if the file does not exist.
LAB_SSH_KEY="${HOME}/.ssh/id_ed25519_anon.pub"

# --- Networking -------------------------------------------------------------
# The NIC layout is per role and fixed by scripts/lib.sh (nic_layout_for_role)
# plus scripts/create-vm.applescript. It is NOT configurable here, because the
# whole security property of this repo depends on it:
#
#   gateway     dual     emulated NAT NIC (internet + the host SSH forward)
#                        AND a host-mode NIC at GATEWAY_INTERNAL_IP.
#   everything  internal ONLY a host-mode NIC on LAB_SEGMENT. No NAT NIC at
#   else                 all, so it has no path to the internet except through
#                        the gateway. Reached from the host by SSH ProxyJump
#                        through the gateway, never by a direct port forward.
#
# The segment is a host-only Apple vmnet switch: no gateway, no route to the
# host's LAN or the internet.
LAB_SEGMENT="10.20.0.0/24"
GATEWAY_INTERNAL_IP="10.20.0.1"

# --- Resource defaults ------------------------------------------------------
# Defaults for every VM in LAB_VMS below. A VM overrides any of these with a
# cpu= / ram= / disk= field in its fleet entry.
LAB_CPU=2
LAB_RAM=2048
LAB_DISK_GB=20

# --- Base images (ARM64 / aarch64) ------------------------------------------
# The gateway runs Debian genericcloud (small, stable router); the workstation
# runs Kali. The base image is chosen per role (see scripts/lib.sh role_image).
#
# Debian publishes SHA512SUMS (not SHA256SUMS) next to its cloud images, so
# DEBIAN_SHA_ALGO tells fetch-images.sh which digest to verify with.
DEBIAN_IMG_URL="https://cloud.debian.org/images/cloud/bookworm/latest/debian-12-genericcloud-arm64.qcow2"
DEBIAN_SHA_URL="https://cloud.debian.org/images/cloud/bookworm/latest/SHA512SUMS"
DEBIAN_SHA_ALGO=512

# Kali workstation image (ARM64 genericcloud, cloud-init enabled). It ships as
# a .tar.xz containing a raw disk (disk.raw); fetch-images.sh verifies the
# archive, extracts it and renames it to KALI_IMG_FILE. The raw image is
# ~25 GiB (already larger than LAB_DISK_GB, so create-vm.sh never shrinks it).
#
# The URLs point at Kali's per-release directory (kali-<version>/), NOT current/.
# current/ only ever holds the newest build, so a pin there 404s the moment Kali
# cuts a release; the versioned directory keeps its image and SHA256SUMS in place
# afterwards. Bumping KALI_VERSION selects the matching directory, so pick any
# release listed at https://kali.download/cloud-images/ (mirror of
# https://www.kali.org/releases/). Very old releases are eventually pruned from
# kali.download to https://old.kali.org/cloud-images/.
KALI_VERSION="2026.2"
KALI_IMG_URL="https://kali.download/cloud-images/kali-${KALI_VERSION}/kali-linux-${KALI_VERSION}-cloud-genericcloud-arm64.tar.xz"
KALI_SHA_URL="https://kali.download/cloud-images/kali-${KALI_VERSION}/SHA256SUMS"
KALI_IMG_FILE="kali-genericcloud-arm64.raw"

# --- VM fleet ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Each entry: "name:role [cpu=N] [ram=MiB] [disk=GB]"
#
#   name   short name: the UTM VM is LAB_PREFIX-name, and this is what
#          'make ssh' and the Ansible inventory use
#   role   maps to a base image (gateway=Debian, anything else=Kali), a NIC
#          layout, a cloud-init seed and an Ansible group
#   cpu    CPU cores       (default: LAB_CPU)
#   ram    memory in MiB   (default: LAB_RAM)
#   disk   disk size in GB (default: LAB_DISK_GB)
#
# The gateway MUST be index 1 (the first entry): its host SSH port is
# 2200+index, and both the workstation's SSH ProxyJump and scripts/verify.sh
# derive that port from index 1.
#
# Changing cpu= or ram= for a VM that already exists makes the next 'make up'
# stop that VM, apply the change, and start it again. VMs whose cpu/ram did
# not change are never restarted.
#
# disk= is only applied when a VM is first created: UTM imports the staged
# disk into its own bundle at creation time, so raising disk= later has no
# effect on a VM that already exists. To grow the disk of an existing VM, run
# 'make destroy' then 'make up'. Disks are never shrunk either way.
#
# The workstation is disposable per assignment: 'make destroy' then 'make up'
# clones it fresh from the base image.
LAB_VMS=(
  "gateway:gateway cpu=2 ram=2048 disk=20"
  "workstation:workstation cpu=4 ram=4096 disk=60"
)
